d 'MMWSMED': module for conducting causal mediation analysis using ratio-of-mediator-probability weighting with parametric or nonparametric weights
d
d  mmwsmed decomposes the total effect of a treatment on an outcome
d into natural direct and indirect effects using
d ratio-of-mediator-probability weighting (RMPW; Hong 2010; Hong,
d Deutsch, and Hill 2015; Hong 2015, chapters 11 to 13).  RMPW
d allows the effect of the mediator on the outcome to differ by
d treatment (a treatment-by-mediator interaction), makes no
d assumption about the distribution of the outcome, and requires no
d model for the outcome. The estimators, the extensions implemented
d here, and their finite-sample performance are described in Linden
d (2026). The syntax follows that of mediate. 
d
d KW: mediation analysis
d KW: ratio-of-mediator-probability weighting
d KW: marginal mean weighting through stratification
d KW: inverse probability of treatment weights
d KW: causal inference
d
d Requires: Stata version 15
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261107
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
f mmwsmed.ado
f mmwsmed.sthlp
f ../r/Riverside.dta
f MMWSMED.pdf
